[{"text":"FCLoopIntegralToPropagators[int, {q1, q2, ...}] is an auxiliary function that converts the loop integral int that depends on the loop momenta q1, q2, ... to a list of propagators and scalar products.","anchor":"fcloopintegraltopropagators"},{"text":"All propagators and scalar products that do not depend on the loop momenta are discarded, unless the Rest option is set to True.","anchor":"fcloopintegraltopropagators"},{"text":"Overview, FCLoopPropagatorsToTopology","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"SFAD[p1] FCLoopIntegralToPropagators[%, {p1}]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(\\text{p1}^2+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{(\\text{p1}^2+i \\eta )}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SFAD[p1, p2] FCLoopIntegralToPropagators[%, {p1, p2}]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(\\text{p1}^2+i \\eta ).(\\text{p2}^2+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{(\\text{p1}^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{(\\text{p2}^2+i \\eta )}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"If the integral contains propagators raised to integer powers, only one propagator will appear in the output.","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"int = SPD[q, p] SFAD[q, q - p, q - p]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{p\\cdot q}{(q^2+i \\eta ).((q-p)^2+i \\eta )^2}\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCLoopIntegralToPropagators[int, {q}]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{(p\\cdot q+i \\eta ),\\frac{1}{(q^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{((q-p)^2+i \\eta )}\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"However, setting the option Tally to True will count the powers of the appearing propagators.","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCLoopIntegralToPropagators[int, {q}, Tally -> True]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left( \\begin{array}{cc} \\frac{1}{(q^2+i \\eta )} & 1 \\\\ (p\\cdot q+i \\eta ) & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{((q-p)^2+i \\eta )} & 2 \\\\ \\end{array} \\right)\\]","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Here is a more realistic 3-loop example","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"int = SFAD[{{-k1, 0}, {mc^2, 1}, 1}] SFAD[{{-k1 - k2, 0}, {mc^2, 1}, 1}] SFAD[{{-k2, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}] SFAD[{{-k2, 0}, {0, 1}, 2}] SFAD[{{-k3, 0}, {mc^2, 1}, 1}] *SFAD[{{k1 - k3 - p1, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}] SFAD[{{-k1 - k2 + k3 + p1, 0}, {0, 1}, 1}] SFAD[{{-k1 - k2 + k3 + p1, 0}, {0, 1}, 2}]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(\\text{k2}^2+i \\eta )^3 (\\text{k1}^2-\\text{mc}^2+i \\eta ) (\\text{k3}^2-\\text{mc}^2+i \\eta ) ((-\\text{k1}-\\text{k2})^2-\\text{mc}^2+i \\eta ) ((\\text{k1}-\\text{k3}-\\text{p1})^2+i \\eta ) ((-\\text{k1}-\\text{k2}+\\text{k3}+\\text{p1})^2+i \\eta )^3}\\]","anchor":"cb6-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCLoopIntegralToPropagators[int, {k1, k2, k3}, Tally -> True]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left( \\begin{array}{cc} \\frac{1}{(\\text{k2}^2+i \\eta )} & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{(\\text{k3}^2-\\text{mc}^2+i \\eta )} & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{(\\text{k1}^2-\\text{mc}^2+i \\eta )} & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{((\\text{k1}-\\text{k3}-\\text{p1})^2+i \\eta )} & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{((-\\text{k1}-\\text{k2}+\\text{k3}+\\text{p1})^2+i \\eta )} & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{((-\\text{k1}-\\text{k2})^2-\\text{mc}^2+i \\eta )} & 1 \\\\ \\end{array} \\right)\\]","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Examples"}]